ERROR REPORTS

Please send errors and suggestions to Frans Kaashoek and Robert Morris
(kaashoek,rtm@mit.edu).  The main purpose of xv6 is as a teaching
operating system for MIT's 6.1810, so we are more interested in
simplifications and clarifications than new features.

BUILDING AND RUNNING XV6

You will need a RISC-V "newlib" tool chain from
https://github.com/riscv/riscv-gnu-toolchain, and qemu compiled for
riscv64-softmmu.  Once they are installed, and in your shell
search path, you can run "make qemu".


ADVANCED KERNEL FEATURES: 

Objective:
Extend the kernel with 10 monitoring, management, and simulation modules
(5 Operating System + 5 Computer Architecture), each with 3 extensions,
so the kernel is observable, measurable, and useful for learning.

Benefits:
- Visibility into processes, memory, and system calls
- Better resource management
- Hands-on architecture learning
- Built-in performance metrics
- Modular design


1. OPERATING SYSTEM MODULES


1. Process Information Module
   Purpose: View PID, process name, and state
   Extensions:
   - Parent-child process tree
   - Per-process CPU time and memory usage
   - Sorting and filtering

2. System Call Counter Module
   Purpose: Count how often each system call is executed
   Extensions:
   - Per-process syscall counters
   - Syscall latency measurement
   - Top-N syscalls with reset and export

3. Memory Usage Monitor
   Purpose: Track used and free memory
   Extensions:
   - Per-process memory usage
   - Fragmentation and page/frame statistics
   - Low-memory threshold warnings

4. File Management Module
   Purpose: Create, read, write, and delete files
   Extensions:
   - Rename, copy, and move
   - File metadata and permissions
   - Directory listing and file search

5. Process Priority Management
   Purpose: Priority-based scheduling
   Extensions:
   - Aging to prevent starvation
   - Multiple scheduling policies (RR, Priority, SJF)
   - Runtime priority change (renice)


2. COMPUTER ARCHITECTURE MODULES


1. Number System Converter
   Purpose: Binary, Decimal, Hexadecimal conversion
   Extensions:
   - Octal and signed numbers (two's complement)
   - Floating-point (IEEE-754) conversion
   - Bit-width selection, endianness view, batch mode

2. Cache Memory Simulator
   Purpose: Simulate cache and show hits and misses
   Extensions:
   - Configurable size, block size, associativity
   - Replacement policies (LRU, FIFO, Random)
   - Multi-level cache (L1/L2) with AMAT report

3. RISC-V Instruction Decoder
   Purpose: Decode opcodes and register information
   Extensions:
   - All formats (R, I, S, B, U, J)
   - Assembly mnemonic output with immediates
   - Batch decoding from hex file and encoder

4. CPU Performance Calculator
   Purpose: Calculate CPI and related metrics
   Extensions:
   - CPU time, MIPS, and clock rate
   - Weighted CPI from instruction mix
   - Speedup comparison (Amdahl's Law)

5. Branch Prediction Simulator
   Purpose: Simulate Taken/Not Taken and compute accuracy
   Extensions:
   - 1-bit and 2-bit saturating-counter predictors
   - History-based predictors (BHT, gshare)
   - Trace-file input and predictor comparison



